   "title": "Newspaper vocabulary added",
   "text": "60,446 of the reference words come from a newspaper corpus (Leipzig Corpora Collection, kan_newscrawl_2016_100K, 1.3 million words); 1,690 come from the subtitle list. Written sources are more formal than subtitles and contain more names and foreign words. Frequencies of the corpus-only words come from that corpus and are not comparable with subtitle frequencies."
  },
  {
   "title": "Abugida: CV and length",
   "text": "Kannada is an abugida: CV (orthographic) counts every consonant letter as C plus an inherent vowel V unless a vowel sign or virama follows; vowel signs and vowel letters are V; anusvara is C. Length is counted in aksharas."
  }
